' File Limits (M4 example): how FILELOAD treats files that do not fit a
' STRING. Reads only. The owner creates the three files on the host first:
'   PBEXACT.TXT  63 letters  -> loaded (the most a 64-byte STRING holds)
'   PBLONG.TXT   64 letters  -> refused: longer than 63 characters
'   PBZERO.TXT   has a zero byte -> refused: not text
DIM Text$ AS STRING
Text$ = "start"
FILELOAD "PBEXACT.TXT", Text$
MESSAGE "PBEXACT gives " + STR$(LEN(Text$)) + " letters"
Text$ = "start"
FILELOAD "PBLONG.TXT", Text$
MESSAGE "After PBLONG: " + Text$
FILELOAD "PBZERO.TXT", Text$
MESSAGE "After PBZERO: " + Text$
END
